            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+vector+bundle"}> universal vector bundle
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+complex+line+bundle"} universal complex line bundle
          %h3#basic_properties Basic properties
          %p metric structure
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structure"} orthogonal structure
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+structure"} Hermitian structure
          %p
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+spaces"} compact topological spaces
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concordance"} concordance
            %li
              %p direct summand of trivial bundle
          %h3#references_2 References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Hatcher"} Hatcher, section 1.1
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Wirthmuller12"} Wirthmuller 12, section 1 and section 3
          %h2#ClassifyingSpaces
            %strong Classifying spaces
          %h3#idea_4 Idea
          %p
            Some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            are “tautological”. For consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            of all
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %em is
            that subspace. It is possible to take this construction and allow
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            to go to infinity. The result is a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            for vector bundles which carries a
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+vector+bundle"} universal vector bundle
            %em classified
            by a map into this classifying space, namely the map that, roughly, sends each point to the lable of the fiber above it.
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+spaces"} classifying spaces
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
          %p We use the above fact (…) that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+bundle"} real vector bundle
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
                to the canonical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated bundle
                to an
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} O(n)
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %li
              %p
                every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundle"} complex vector bundle
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
                to the canonical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated bundle
                to an
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} U(n)
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
          %h3#grassmannian_spaces Grassmannian spaces
          %p
            In the following we take
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            to denote
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times (-)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            and hence preserves
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
          #StiefelManifold.num_defn
            %h6#definition_31 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n, k \in \mathbb{N}
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \leq k
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %strong
                real
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stiefel+manifold"} Stiefel manifold
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^k
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset"} coset
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V_n(\mathbb{R}^k) \coloneqq O(k)/O(k-n)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(k-n)
              is via its canonical embedding
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(k-n)\hookrightarrow O(k)
            %p
              Similarly the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %strong complex Stiefel manifold
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^k
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V_n(\mathbb{C}^k) \coloneqq U(k)/U(k-n)
                    \\,,
            %p
              here the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(k-n)
              is via its canonical embedding
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(k-n)\hookrightarrow U(k)
          #RealAndComplexGrassmannian.num_defn
            %h6#definition_32 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
