                    O(n) Bund/_\sim
            %p
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
              of functions from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B O(n)
              and isomorphism classes of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            A full proof is spelled out in (
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher"}> Hatcher, section 1.2, theorem 1.16
            )
          %h3#references_3 References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Hatcher"} Hatcher, section 1.2
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Wirthmuller12"} Wirthmuller 12, section 2
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#AguilarGitlerPrieto02"} Aguilar-Gitler-Prieto 02, sections 8.3-8-5
          %h2#KTheoryRing
            %strong
              The K-theory functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^\bullet(-)
          %h3#idea_5 Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            over some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            naturally form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
            (in fact a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
          %p
            There is a universal way to turn a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
            into an actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            by adjoining formal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverses"} inverses
            to all elements. This is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group"} Grothendieck group
            construction. Applying this to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            yields “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+vector+bundles"}> virtual vector bundles
            ”, which are formal differences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [E] - [F]
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
            of actual vector bundles. These now form an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            group of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
          %p
            Since for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \;\colon\; X \to Y
            and every vector bundle over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            there is the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+bundle"} pullback bundle
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contravariant+functor"} contravariant
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+topological+spaces"} category of topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            groups are. In the next session we see that this analogy goes further, so we also call
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
            the
            %em K-cohomology group
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            In fact
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
            has more structure than just that of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+bundles"} tensor product of vector bundles
            makes it a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theory"} multiplicative cohomology theory
          %h3#references_4 References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Wirthmuller12"} Wirthmuller 12, sections 6 and 10
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Hatcher"} Hatcher, section 2.1
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#AguilarGitlerPrieto02"} Aguilar-Gitler-Prieto 02, section 9
          %h2#GeneralizedCohomology
            %strong Generalized cohomology
          %h3#idea_6 Idea
          %p
            We may now make precise in which sense the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(-)
            is directly analogous to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            functors
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^\bullet(-,\mathbb{Z})
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cones"} mapping cones
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspensions"} suspensions
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequences+in+cohomology"} long exact sequences in cohomology
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p There are two versions of the statement of the axioms:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a{:href => "#ReducedCohomology"} Reduced cohomology
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a{:href => "#UnreducedCohomology"} Unreduced cohomology
                \.
          %p
            There are functors taking any reduced cohomology theory to an unreduced one, and vice versa. When some fine detail in the axioms is suitably set up, then this establishes an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
            between reduced and unreduced generalized cohomology:
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#RelationBetweenReducedAndUnreduced"} Relation between reduced and unreduced cohomology
          %h3#mapping_cones Mapping cones
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cylinder"} mapping cylinder
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cone"} mapping cone
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofiber"} homotopy cofiber
          %h3#ReducedCohomology Reduced cohomology
          %p
            Throughout, write
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi CW
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_{CW}
            for the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Top
                    %mi CW
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}_{CW}
            for the corresponding category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
          %p
            Recall that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Top
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}
            are computed as colimits in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            after adjoining the base point and its inclusion maps to the given diagram
          #WedgeSumAsCoproduct.num_example
            %h6#example_12 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
              is the
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∨
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee_{i \in I} X_i
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Top
                    %mi CW
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Top
                    %mi CW
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma \coloneqq S^1 \wedge (-)
                  \\;\colon\;
                  Top^{\ast/}_{CW} \longrightarrow Top^{\ast/}_{CW}
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+suspension"} reduced suspension
            functor.
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ab
                    %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab^{\mathbb{Z}}
            for the category of integer-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+abelian+groups"}> graded abelian groups
            \.
          #ReducedGeneralizedCohomology.num_defn
            %h6#definition_36 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                reduced
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mi CW
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi Ab
                      %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tilde E^\bullet
                    \\;\colon\;
                    (Top^{\ast/}_{CW})^{op} \longrightarrow Ab^{\mathbb{Z}}
            %p
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"}> CW-complexes
              ) to
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+abelian+groups"} graded abelian groups
              (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+groups"}> cohomology groups
              ”), in components
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi f
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tilde E
                    \\;\colon\;
                    (X \stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow} Y)
                    \\mapsto
                    (\tilde E^\bullet(Y)
                    \\stackrel{f^\ast}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\tilde E^\bullet(X))
                    \\,,
            %p
              and equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              of degree +1, to be called the
              = succeed "," do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+isomorphism"} suspension isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\tilde E^{\bullet +1}(\Sigma -)
                    \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\tilde E^\bullet(-)
            %p such that:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %strong
                    (
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+invariance"}> homotopy invariance
                    )
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1,f_2 \colon X \longrightarrow Y
                  are two morphisms of pointed topological spaces such that there is a (base point preserving)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1 \simeq f_2
                  between them, then the induced
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
                  of abelian groups are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equal
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                          %mo *
                        %mo =
                        %msubsup
                          %mi f
                          %mn 2
                          %mo *
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        f_1^\ast = f_2^\ast
                        \\,.
              %li#ReducedExactnessAxiom
                %p
                  %strong (exactness)
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi A
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon A \hookrightarrow X
                  an inclusion of pointed topological spaces, with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Cone
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \colon X \longrightarrow Cone(i)
                  the induced
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cone"} mapping cone
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
                  of graded abelian groups
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
