          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              The constructions of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedToUnreducedGeneralizedCohomology"}
              and def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FromUnreducedToReducedCohomology"}
              constitute a pair of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              between then
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
              of reduced cohomology theories, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedGeneralizedCohomology"}
              and unreduced cohomology theories, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralizedCohomologyTheory"}
              which exhbit an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          .proof
            %h6#proof_18 Proof
            %p (…careful with checking the respect for suspension iso and connecting homomorphism..)
            %p
              To see that there are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
              relating the two composites of these two functors to the identity:
            %p One composite is
            .maruku-equation
